# The WAL admits a re-presented generation against the initiator's entry alone,
# ignoring its routing floor (#5697 review, S1). A cross-shard straddler: shard root
# s2 of the purged incarnation admitted a write whose keys, under the re-created
# tree's shard map, belong to L. L's first initialisation claims only its own shard
# root's generation (and the range-delete fence's), not s2's, and s2's re-created
# counterpart has not initialised (or no longer exists). With s2's entry retired,
# only the WAL-side floor refuses the write; without it, the write is admitted above
# L's recorded heads and L advances past it. The floor is load-bearing.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestRoutingWalIgnoresFloor
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the WAL admits a re-presented routing generation at or below the initiator's floor
PERTURBS: SAlloc
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithSecondInitiator = TRUE, WithLegacyPurge = FALSE, WithDuplicate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ spStamp >= SEntry
    /\ spStamp > SFloor
    /\ sp' = "none"
--- REPLACE
    /\ spStamp >= SEntry
\* MUTATION: no WAL-side floor check.
    /\ sp' = "none"
--- END
